(Track B2 — mremap realloc path. A dynamic buffer is resized up by ~1 MB,
 exercising the mremap grow path of _realloc_buffer, then down to 5 bytes,
 exercising the alloc plus copy shrink fallback. Asserts data is preserved
 across both and capacity follows the requested size.)

Create a buffer called b.
Append "hello mremap world" to b.

Resize b to 1000000 bytes.
If b's capacity is equal to 1000000 then,
  print "grow cap ok".
Otherwise,
  print "BUG: grow cap".
If b is "hello mremap world" then,
  print "grow data ok".
Otherwise,
  print "BUG: grow data".

Resize b to 5 bytes.
If b's capacity is equal to 5 then,
  print "shrink cap ok".
Otherwise,
  print "BUG: shrink cap".
If b is "hello" then,
  print "shrink data ok".
Otherwise,
  print "BUG: shrink data".